1. Definitions and Scope

1.1. "Agreement" means this Axion Non-Commercial Research and Responsible Use
License, Version 1.0, including Schedule A (Acceptable Use and Safety Policy),
which forms an integral and binding part of this Agreement.
1.2. "Licensor" means the ByteDance legal entity named above, acting only in
respect of intellectual-property rights that it owns or is authorized to
license.
1.3. "Covered Materials" means the following materials expressly identified by
Licensor as released under this Agreement:
(a) "Paper": research papers, manuscripts, technical reports, figures, tables,
and supplementary materials associated with the Axion project, but only to the
extent Licensor possesses the rights necessary to license them under this
Agreement;
(b) "Code": Axion source code, scripts, configurations, training and inference
software, evaluation code, and associated documentation distributed by
Licensor; and
(c) "Models": Axion model architectures as embodied in distributed materials,
model weights, checkpoints, tokenizers, and model-related files distributed by
Licensor.
"Covered Materials" does not include third-party libraries, datasets,
pretrained components, third-party papers, or other materials identified as
subject to separate terms. Merely referencing another work does not bring that
work within this Agreement.
1.4. "Derivative Materials" means versions of Covered Materials that are
modified, adapted, fine-tuned, quantized, pruned, merged, or otherwise
transformed, and models distilled from the Models or developed using their
outputs as training signals. This definition describes the contractual scope of
permitted use; it does not imply that Licensor owns copyrights in independently
protectable contributions or in content in which no such rights exist.
1.5. "Outputs" means text, images, code, data, actions, or other results
produced through use of the Code or Models, including results produced when
those systems use external tools.
1.6. "Non-Commercial Research Purposes" means independent academic research,
education, personal learning, reproducibility studies, scientific evaluation,
and responsible AI safety research that are not conducted for, directed toward,
or intended to provide a direct or indirect commercial advantage or financial
benefit to a business or other commercial undertaking.
1.7. "Commercial Use" means any use, exploitation, or distribution for a
business purpose or direct or indirect commercial advantage, whether or not
fees are charged or revenue is immediately generated. It includes, without
limitation: use by or on behalf of a for-profit organization in its business or
internal research; product development, commercialization, and market
evaluation; use in paid or ad-supported products or services; API, hosted, or
model-as-a-service offerings; customer or client work; commercial training,
fine-tuning, or distillation; paid licensing or resale; and use under an
arrangement designed to give a commercial sponsor exclusive or preferential
business benefit.
Ordinary personal activity by an individual employed by a business is not
automatically Commercial Use if undertaken independently, without employer
direction or resources, and without a commercial purpose. Using ordinary paid
computing, storage, or repository-hosting services to carry out otherwise
permitted non-commercial research does not, by itself, turn the Licensee's
research into Commercial Use; however, this sentence grants no right to any
service provider to independently exploit the Covered Materials commercially.
1.8. "You" or "Licensee" means the individual or entity exercising rights under
this Agreement. If an individual acts on behalf of an entity, that entity must
independently be eligible to accept and comply with this Agreement.

