9. Termination

9.1. Your rights under this Agreement terminate automatically upon Your breach
of any license condition, including the prohibition on Commercial Use or any
provision of Schedule A, subject to limitations imposed by applicable law.
9.2. Upon termination, You must immediately cease unlicensed access, use,
modification, and distribution of the Covered Materials and related Derivative
Materials and, within 30 days, delete or destroy copies in Your control, except
to the extent retention is required by law. Any legally required retained
copies must not be used or distributed except as permitted by law.
9.3. Termination does not eliminate liabilities arising before termination and
does not terminate independent permissions validly granted by Licensor to
compliant third parties. Sections 4.3 (as to Outputs created before
termination), 7, 9, 10, 11, 12, and 13 survive to the extent legally
applicable.

