Schedule A - Acceptable Use and Safety Policy

This Schedule A is part of the License, not an optional set of
recommendations. You must not use or knowingly enable others to use Covered
Materials, Derivative Materials, or tools and applications built with them for
any of the following purposes:

A1. Illegal acts and violations of rights. Committing, facilitating, planning,
or materially assisting unlawful acts; violating intellectual-property,
privacy, data-protection, confidentiality, or other applicable legal rights; or
obtaining access to systems or information without authorization.
A2. Violence and dangerous capabilities. Facilitating terrorism, violent
extremism, violent crime, or serious physical harm; developing, acquiring, or
deploying unlawful weapons; or materially enabling the design, acquisition, or
misuse of chemical, biological, radiological, or nuclear weapons or other
capabilities intended to cause mass harm.
A3. Child exploitation and sexual abuse. Creating, distributing, soliciting, or
facilitating child sexual abuse material, sexual exploitation or abuse of
minors, human trafficking, non-consensual intimate imagery, or sexual violence.
A4. Malicious cyber activity. Unauthorized intrusion, credential theft, malware
deployment, destructive cyber operations, unauthorized surveillance of
networks, exfiltration of information, or automation of such conduct.
Authorized security testing in controlled environments is permitted under
Section 6.4 only when it does not cause unauthorized harm.
A5. Privacy-invasive identification or surveillance. Unlawful collection,
disclosure, profiling, tracking, or identification of individuals;
non-consensual biometric identification or sensitive-personal-data processing;
or mass surveillance in violation of human rights or applicable law.
A6. Fraud, deception, manipulation, and harassment. Scams, identity theft,
deceptive impersonation, targeted intimidation, stalking, harassment, or
deliberate misinformation that foreseeably creates significant real-world harm;
or manipulation designed to undermine individuals' informed decision-making in
consequential settings.
A7. Discrimination and denial of rights. Unlawful discrimination, persecution,
or targeting of persons based on protected or sensitive characteristics; or
systems designed to deny rights or opportunities on an unlawful discriminatory
basis.
A8. Unsafe high-stakes decision-making. Using a Model as an unsupervised or
final decision-maker in medical care, mental health crisis response, legal
determinations, employment, housing, credit, insurance, education admissions,
migration, policing, or other consequential decisions affecting individuals'
rights, safety, or livelihood. Controlled, non-commercial research on such
applications is allowed only without real-world consequential deployment and
with appropriate ethical and legal safeguards.
A9. Uncontrolled autonomous agents. Deploying agentic systems that autonomously
access third-party services, execute transactions, alter external systems, or
take consequential real-world actions without appropriate authorization, access
scoping, monitoring, human oversight, and emergency-stop mechanisms
proportionate to the risk.
A10. Evasion or enabling prohibited uses. Intentionally bypassing safety
mechanisms, access controls, license restrictions, or evaluations for the
purpose of enabling a prohibited use; or distributing adaptations specifically
intended to facilitate the prohibited activities above.

Minimum Responsible-Use Requirements

For every permitted use, You must, as appropriate to the foreseeable risks and
capabilities involved:

B1. Evaluate material safety, security, robustness, and misuse risks before
releasing derivatives or applications.
B2. Provide meaningful human oversight, authorization controls, rate limits,
and technical safeguards when enabling tool use or external actions.
B3. Respect data minimization, confidentiality, security, privacy, and
applicable retention requirements.
B4. Document known limitations and avoid representing experimental outputs as
verified facts, professional advice, or safety guarantees.
B5. Promptly investigate and mitigate significant safety or security incidents
within Your control and comply with applicable incident-reporting laws.
B6. Ensure recipients receive this Agreement, including Schedule A, when
redistribution is permitted.

Research exception clarification. This Schedule does not prohibit good-faith,
non-commercial study of safety failures, model bias, harmful-content detection,
or defensive security when conducted in authorized and appropriately contained
settings. It does prohibit causing actual harm or deploying prohibited
capabilities under the pretext of research.
